<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- The setting that makes the console's MAP tab exist.

     Setup > Field Service Settings > "Send geolocation and map data to Google
     and Apple". Off by default, and with it off the Dispatcher Console shows
     GANTT and no MAP tab, without an error.

     It lives here rather than in field-service/ for two reasons. It is only
     of use with the managed package - the map is the package's - and this
     directory is the one setup.sh deploys once it has confirmed the package
     is there. And field-service/ is deployed only on an org where Field
     Service was off, so a setting placed there would never reach an org that
     already had it on.

     What it does is what it says: Field Service may send addresses and
     coordinates to Google and Apple to draw maps and geocode. That is how
     the map is drawn at all. An org where that is not acceptable should not
     have this on, and will not have the map. -->
<FieldServiceSettings xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <canPopulateGoogleAddress>true</canPopulateGoogleAddress>
</FieldServiceSettings>
